# Baron Strucker, HYDRA Overlord: "Do this only once each turn" (CR 603.2h) when control of him changes while his triggers
# wait. On turn 5 Agents of HYDRA enters under Bot1 (a trigger), and in response Bot1 flashes in Swarm, Being of Bees (a
# second trigger, above it). With both waiting, Bot2 takes Baron with Old Man of the Sea. Both triggers are still Bot1's
# (CR 603.3a) and their "you" is Bot1: the second resolves and Bot1 has Swarm connive (an Ornithopter discarded: a +1/+1
# counter) - Bot1's doing, though Bot2 controls Baron by then. The first finds Bot1 has connived with Baron this turn and
# asks nothing, so Agents stays 1/1. Bot2, Baron's controller now, has not: Bot2's own Swarm, flashed in after, triggers
# for Bot2 and connives (a Swamp discarded, no counter).

